Description: "3D display settings..." starts KScreen's page on the desktop session's platform
 The View menu's "3D display settings..." started kcmshell6 with ParaView's own environment. When ParaView runs on
 xcb inside a Wayland session (QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb, the GLX route), KScreen's page ran on xcb too, asked for the X11
 backend, whose service aborted ("Process org.kde.KScreen received signal 6"), and the page said that no KScreen
 backend was found. kcmshell6 is now started without QT_QPA_PLATFORM, so the page follows the session.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
---
--- a/Clients/ParaView/ParaViewMainWindow.cxx
+++ b/Clients/ParaView/ParaViewMainWindow.cxx
@@ -359,7 +359,15 @@
   QObject::connect(displaySettings, &QAction::triggered, this,
     [this]()
     {
-      if (!QProcess::startDetached(QStringLiteral("kcmshell6"), { QStringLiteral("kcm_kscreen") }))
+      // KScreen's page follows the desktop session, not ParaView: started with ParaView's QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb inside a
+      // Wayland session it asks for the X11 backend, which aborts, and the page has no display to show.
+      QProcess settings;
+      settings.setProgram(QStringLiteral("kcmshell6"));
+      settings.setArguments({ QStringLiteral("kcm_kscreen") });
+      QProcessEnvironment environment = QProcessEnvironment::systemEnvironment();
+      environment.remove(QStringLiteral("QT_QPA_PLATFORM"));
+      settings.setProcessEnvironment(environment);
+      if (!settings.startDetached())
       {
         QMessageBox::warning(this, QStringLiteral("ParaView"),
           QString::fromUtf8(vtkPVStereoEdition::Text("The display settings could not be opened.")));
